{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a15342-a65f-75ee-a2d0-57aea1f06aee","toolName":"task","args":{},"result":"{\"lg_name\":\"Command\",\"update\":{\"files\":{},\"messages\":[{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"content\":\"## Source\\n/home/user/app/contracts/SwarmTypes.sol  \\n/home/user/app/contracts/DealFactory.sol  \\n/home/user/app/contracts/DemandPool.sol  \\n/home/user/app/contracts/Settler.sol\\n\\n## Action\\ncreated\\n\\n## Survey\\n- `survey_solidity_contracts` returned no `candidates`.\\n- `survey_solidity_contracts` returned no `hidden` paths.\\n- I worked on these new paths:\\n  - `/home/user/app/contracts/SwarmTypes.sol`\\n  - `/home/user/app/contracts/DealFactory.sol`\\n  - `/home/user/app/contracts/DemandPool.sol`\\n  - `/home/user/app/contracts/Settler.sol`\\n\\n## Summary\\n- Created new Solidity sources under `/home/user/app/contracts/` because no related Solidity existed in survey results.\\n- Started from an OpenZeppelin scaffold via `solidity-custom` (as required for CREATE path), then implemented the full 4-file Swarm system to your specification with manual owner logic (no OZ Ownable import).\\n- Implemented `SwarmTypes` exactly with `Tier` and `Deal` structs and required field widths/state encoding.\\n- Implemented `DealFactory` with tier validation, price cap and buyer cap enforcement, pause/unpause, ownership transfer, `getDeal`, one-time `setSettler`/`setDemandPool`, and settler-only `setDealState` enforcing `0 -> 1` or `0 -> 2`.\\n- Implemented `DemandPool` with `ReentrancyGuard`, commit/withdraw escrow logic in USDC micro-units, post-add clearing-price commit pricing, swap-and-pop buyer removal with index maintenance, tier-break event emission, buyer/escrow getters, and settler-only `pullForSettler`.\\n- Implemented `Settler` with `ReentrancyGuard`, deadline-gated mutually exclusive `settle`/`refundAll`, claimable credit accounting (accumulating across deals), direct pool-to-claimant payout path in `claim`, and explicit conservation assertion in `settle`.\\n- Included the required key-constraint comment block in each main contract and avoided `msg.value` and `block.prevrandao`; used `block.timestamp` only for deadline comparisons.\",\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_012VkEm6AAq7gi38CyrcFKYs\",\"name\":\"task\",\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}]},\"goto\":[]}"}}
