{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a15345-c72c-7695-8377-44c55b75e242","toolName":"task","args":{},"result":"{\"lg_name\":\"Command\",\"update\":{\"files\":{},\"filesReadTrace\":[\"/home/user/app/contracts/SwarmTypes.sol\",\"/home/user/app/contracts/DealFactory.sol\",\"/home/user/app/contracts/DemandPool.sol\",\"/home/user/app/contracts/Settler.sol\"],\"messages\":[{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"content\":\"High — `emit-events-access-control` — Administrative role and control-plane changes do not emit events\\n**Location:** DealFactory.sol:95, DealFactory.pause\\n**Why it matters:** `pause`, `unpause`, `transferOwnership`, `setDemandPool`, and `setSettler` all change privileged control state but emit no events (same pattern also appears in `DemandPool.setSettler` and `Settler.pause/unpause/transferOwnership`). Without event logs, monitoring/alerting systems cannot reliably detect governance or control-plane changes in real time, which weakens incident response and post-incident forensics.\\n**Fix:** Emit explicit events on every access-control or privileged-config mutation (including ownership transfer and one-time controller wiring), e.g. `OwnershipTransferred(oldOwner,newOwner)`, `Paused(account)`, `Unpaused(account)`, `DemandPoolSet(addr)`, `SettlerSet(addr)`.\\n\\nHigh — `critical-paths-missing-whennotpaused` — Settler exposes pause controls but does not gate critical state-changing flows\\n**Location:** Settler.sol:60, Settler.settle\\n**Why it matters:** `Settler` has `paused` state plus `pause()/unpause()`, but `settle`, `refundAll`, and `claim` do not check `paused`. This creates a false safety control: operators may believe they can halt settlement/refund/claim operations during emergencies, but the critical paths remain fully executable. In a live incident, this can prevent expected containment actions.\\n**Fix:** Apply a consistent pause guard to intended emergency-stoppable critical functions (e.g., `whenNotPaused`-style modifier or explicit `if (paused) revert Paused();`) and define which paths are intentionally exempt.\\n\\n## Files Read\\n| File | Read |\\n|---|---|\\n| /home/user/app/contracts/SwarmTypes.sol | yes |\\n| /home/user/app/contracts/DealFactory.sol | yes |\\n| /home/user/app/contracts/DemandPool.sol | yes |\\n| /home/user/app/contracts/Settler.sol | yes |\\n\\n## Audit Provenance\\n| Subagent | Dispatched | Files audited | Corpus rules cited |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| solidity-auditor | yes | 4 | emit-events-access-control, critical-paths-missing-whennotpaused |\",\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_012kmLfZEvUf5PhoYGnG9EYf\",\"name\":\"task\",\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}]},\"goto\":[]}"}}
