{"kind":"data","event":{"type":"tool_call","status":"complete","toolCallId":"01a15345-c731-75ac-9db3-dfc0bdc44c68","toolName":"task","args":{},"result":"{\"lg_name\":\"Command\",\"update\":{\"files\":{},\"messages\":[{\"lc\":1,\"type\":\"constructor\",\"id\":[\"langchain_core\",\"messages\",\"ToolMessage\"],\"kwargs\":{\"content\":\"## Findings\\n1. [Critical] `settlement-can-brick-after-tier-break` — withdrawals can leave buyers who paid below final clearing price, causing `settle()` revert and permanent fund lock\\n   Criterion: 2 adversary-resistant\\n   Location: `contracts/Settler.sol:Settler.settle` (approx line 79), coupled with `contracts/DemandPool.sol:DemandPool.withdraw` (approx lines 119–134)\\n   Why it matters: `settle()` computes `refund = uint256(paid) - cp`. If withdrawals before deadline increase the clearing price (`cp`) above what some remaining buyer originally paid, this subtraction underflows and reverts. In that state, `settle()` cannot execute, and if `minBuyers` is still met then `refundAll()` is also disallowed, so escrowed USDC can become permanently stuck.\\n   Suggested fix: Ensure each remaining buyer’s escrow is brought up to the current live clearing price whenever price increases (e.g., force top-up on price increases, or track per-buyer obligations differently), or redesign settlement math so it never assumes `paid >= final cp` for all remaining buyers. Add tests for join→unlock-lower-tier→partial-withdraw→higher-final-price scenarios.\\n\\n## Assumptions\\n- Assumed Arc Testnet is the deployment target (as specified), and that USDC at `0x3600000000000000000000000000000000000000` is the intended token.\\n- Assumed “commit escrows CURRENT tier price” means the price at commit-time for that buyer, not a continuously adjusted escrow unless explicitly topped up.\\n\\n## Audit Provenance\\n| Subagent | Dispatched | Files audited | Corpus rules cited |\\n|---|---|---|---|\\n| functional-auditor | yes | 4 | — |\",\"tool_call_id\":\"toolu_bdrk_01KEv29YDEcj3vovZP18BsT2\",\"name\":\"task\",\"additional_kwargs\":{},\"response_metadata\":{}}}]},\"goto\":[]}"}}
